# Template for .env -- copy to `.env` and fill in. `.env` is gitignored; this
# file is committed and must never contain a real token.
#
#     cp .env.example .env
#
# One account per numbered block, contiguous from 1. Rotation order is numeric:
# tools/kaggle_client.py starts at the lowest-numbered account that is not in
# quota cooldown and moves down the list as each one is exhausted. A gap in the
# numbering truncates the list rather than renumbering it, so do not leave one.
#
# USERNAME and TOKEN must belong to the same account. They are used together --
# a kernel is pushed to <USERNAME>/<slug> with <TOKEN> as the Bearer credential,
# so a mismatched pair pushes into an account the token cannot write to.
#
# Tokens are Kaggle's newer KGAT_ format (Bearer auth); see the header of
# tools/kaggle_client.py for why the classic `kaggle` CLI rejects them. Get one
# from kaggle.com -> Settings -> API -> Create New Token.
#
# Each account has its own 30 GPU-h weekly allowance on a rolling seven-day
# window, so adding an account here is what buys more compute. One account is
# enough to run everything; the second only shortens the wait.
#
# Note that a kernel's *output* is visible only to the account that produced it.
# A stage that mounts another kernel (tools/finish.py's b2_eval) is pinned to
# that kernel's owner and does not rotate.

KAGGLE_ACCOUNT_1_USERNAME=your-kaggle-username
KAGGLE_ACCOUNT_1_TOKEN=KGAT_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx

KAGGLE_ACCOUNT_2_USERNAME=your-second-kaggle-username
KAGGLE_ACCOUNT_2_TOKEN=KGAT_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx
